# Normalize line endings automatically for text files (LF in the repo).
* text=auto

# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers. Force LF so a Windows checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true) never rewrites the shebang to "#!/bin/bash\r", which
# makes the container fail with "no such file or directory".
*.sh text eol=lf

# The browser fixtures are byte-exact evidence: their CRLF terminators ARE the
# property under test (a bare LF moves down without returning to column 0, so
# an LF-only transcript stair-steps across the screen instead of scrolling it).
# `* text=auto` above normalised them to LF on the first commit, which would
# have handed a fresh clone bytes the server never sends -- measured
# 2026-09-18, the blob held LF while the working file held CRLF.
tests/fixtures/*.txt -text
